0007:     """Draw the red trace from its border marker, detouring around each blue/green bar it hits.
0008: 
0009:     Input structure
0010:     - The grid has a background, one red marker on the border, and blue/green
0011:       one-cell-thick bars perpendicular to the marker's inward direction.
0012: 
0013:     Rule
0014:     - The red marker travels straight inward from its border.
0015:     - When the trace hits a blue bar, it passes around the bar on the left side
0016:       relative to its direction of travel.
0017:     - When the trace hits a green bar, it passes around the bar on the right
0018:       side relative to its direction of travel.
0019:     - Existing bars are preserved; only background cells on the trace become red.
0020: 
0021:     Key insight
0022:     - The trace keeps the same overall forward direction; each hit bar only
0023:       shifts the current lane by forcing a detour one cell before the obstacle.
0024:     """
0025:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
0026:     h, w = g.shape
0027:     bg = get_bg(g)
0028:     red = Color.RED
0029:     blue = Color.BLUE
0030:     green = Color.GREEN
0031:     assert set(map(int, np.unique(g))) <= {bg, red, blue, green}
0032: 
0033:     starts = np.argwhere(g == red)
0034:     assert starts.shape == (1, 2)
